Tuscan Bean and Pumpkin Soup
  --KitchenAid

Parsley Pesto:
1/2 c walnuts
2 cloves garlic
4 c fresh Italian parsley
1/2 - 3/4 c olive oil
1/2 c grated Parmesan cheese
1/2 tsp fresh ground black pepper

Place walnuts and garlic in work bowl of a food processor and pulse 3-4 times until finely chopped. Remove walnuts into separate bowl. Add parsley and pulse until finely minced. Return chopped walnuts and garlic to work bowl and pulse 2-3 times to combine. With Food Processor running on low speed, pour olive oil into narrow feed tube so oil slowly drizzles into pesto. Transfer pesto to medium bowl and stir in Parmesan cheese and black pepper to taste. Set aside until ready to use. Can be made 2 days ahead and stored in refrigerator.

Soup:
2 carrots, peeled and cut into 1-inch sections
1 rib celery, cut into 1-inch sections
1 medium onion, cut into wedges
2 small redskin potatoes, peeled and cut into quarters
2 cloves garlic
2 tbsp olive oil
2x15.5 oz cannellini beans, drained and rinsed
1 1/2 c pumpkin, peeled and cut into 2" chunks (can substitute butternut squash)
14.5 oz chopped tomatoes
2-3 c vegetable stock or water
1 sprig rosemary
1 bay leaf
1 tsp sea salt

Clean work bowl of Food Processor and attach multipurpose blade. One at a time, process carrots, celery, onion, potatoes and garlic pulsing 3-4 times to coarsely chop. Heat olive oil in large stock pot over medium heat. Add carrots, celery, onion and garlic and sauté 2-3 min. Add cannellini beans and enough water to cover and simmer ~15 min until potatoes are cooked. Let cool slightly then puree 1/2 of the soup base in food processor. Return to pot. Wipe out bowl of processor and add pumpkin, pulsing 3-4 times to roughly chop. Add chopped pumpkin, tomatoes, vegetable stock, rosemary, bay leaf and salt. Simmer over low heat until pumpkin is tender, ~15 min. Add chard and cook 2-3 min. Stir in parsley and season with black pepper to taste. Pour soup into bowls and top with a 1-2 tsp of the parsley pesto. 


